jobs.description:
As a Logistics Employee, you will be part of a team that keeps warehouse operations running smoothly. Depending on your experience and interests, you can work in different departments.

🔧 Tools Department

In the Tools department, you work with specialized equipment and materials.

Your tasks may include:

- Checking tools and materials;
- Scanning products into the system;
- Managing stock levels;
- Preparing materials for shipment;
- Maintaining an organized workspace.

📥 Inbound Department

As an Inbound Employee, you process incoming goods and make sure everything is stored correctly.

Your responsibilities include:

- Receiving deliveries;
- Checking products and quantities;
- Scanning goods into the system;
- Storing products in the correct warehouse locations.

📦 Outbound Department

In Outbound, you make sure customer orders are ready to leave the warehouse.

Your tasks include:

- Picking orders;
- Checking products;
- Packing shipments;
- Preparing orders for transport.

🚜 Reach Truck Positions

Do you have reach truck experience or would you like to develop these skills?

As a Reach Truck Operator, you will:

- Move products throughout the warehouse;
- Replenish stock;
- Pick orders from warehouse racks;
- Work safely at height.

Don't have a certificate yet? Olympia can help you obtain one.

- You are available to work in a 2-shift schedule;
- You speak English, Dutch, or Polish;
- You are motivated and reliable;
- You enjoy working in a team;
- Warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.

Are you a hands-on worker with an eye for detail? Do you enjoy working in a dynamic environment where you can truly make a difference? Then this is your chance to join a leading international company in the world of excavators!

What are you going to do?
As a Logistics Employee, you are an essential link in the logistics operation. You ensure smooth goods flows and make sure everything is processed neatly, safely, and efficiently.

Your tasks:

- Loading, unloading, receiving, and inspecting goods (possibly using a forklift)
- Entering goods into the system and storing them correctly
- Collecting orders and delivering them on time to the correct location
- Ensuring safety, quality, and order in the warehouse
- Actively contributing ideas for process improvements
- Collaborating with colleagues from various departments

What do we offer?
- A varied job at a renowned international organization;
- A competitive salary between € 17 and € 18,50 gross an hour;
- Travel allowance of €0.25 per km;
- Immediate participation in our pension scheme;
- Access to the online Adecco Academy – an online platform with 150+ e-learnings and courses.

Where will you work?
At Hitachi Construction Machinery (Europe), you will be part of the logistics team behind powerful and innovative construction machines. From the warehouse in Amsterdam, we ensure that parts, materials, and machines are delivered worldwide in perfect condition.

What do we ask?
- Good command of Dutch or English;
- Experience in logistics;
- Experience as a forklift driver – Note: a valid certificate is required;
- Good physical condition;
- Accurate working style and adherence to procedures.

Are you interested?
Are you ready to take the next step in your career? Apply now! More questions you can always call Bastiaan Roele by phone 06-52367235
